package com.github.piotr.rusin.yule;
Reason: This package declaration in the test class directory does not match the actual main application package `com.github.piotr_rusin.yule`. Spring Boot's test context loader uses the test class's package as the starting point for component scanning to locate the `@SpringBootApplication`-annotated configuration class. Since the test package is placed outside (or in a sibling location to) the main application's package hierarchy, the scan fails to discover the application configuration, causing a context initialization error.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
package com.github.piotr_rusin.yule;
Reason: By renaming the test package to match the main application's package (`com.github.piotr_rusin.yule`), the test class is now located within the same package hierarchy as the `@SpringBootApplication` main class. This allows Spring Boot's component scanning mechanism to correctly locate the application configuration when initializing the test context, resolving the initialization error.

